IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 5 — Management and Administration`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 5, ss 142–201.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- Part 5 is the largest Part. This encoding covers the computable rules
-- in Divisions 1–5 (Office/Name, Directors/Officers, Meetings, Registers,
-- Annual Return). Purely administrative steps are noted in comments.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Division 1 — Office and name`


§§§ `s 142 — Registered office`

-- s 142(1): every company must have a registered office in Singapore
-- s 142(2): 14-day notice to Registrar of any change
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 142(2)"
`registered office change notice days` MEANS 14


§§§ `s 144 — Publication of name and registration number`

-- s 144(3): penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 144(3)"
`penalty for name publication default` MEANS 1000


§§ `Division 2 — Directors and officers`


§§§ `s 145 — Minimum director requirements`

-- s 145(1): at least one director ordinarily resident in Singapore
-- s 145(2): director must be natural person, aged >= 18
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 145(1)–(2)"
GIVEN `has sg resident director`  IS A BOOLEAN
    , `director age`              IS A NUMBER
    , `director is natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets director requirements` IF
        `has sg resident director`
    AND `director is natural person`
    AND `director age` AT LEAST 18

-- s 145(5): liability after operating > 6 months without SG-resident director
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 145(5)"
`months without sg resident director before member liability` MEANS 6


§§§ `s 147 — Director share qualification`

-- s 147(1): must obtain qualification within 2 months of appointment
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 147(1)"
`director share qualification period months` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 149 — Disqualification of unfit directors of insolvent companies`

-- s 149(1): court may disqualify for up to 5 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 149(1)"
`maximum disqualification years for unfit director` MEANS 5

-- s 149(1): trigger window — director during or within 3 years before liquidation
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 149(1)"
`unfit director lookback years` MEANS 3

-- s 149(3): minimum notice to respondent
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 149(3)"
`unfit director disqualification notice days` MEANS 14


§§§ `s 154 — Disqualification on conviction`

-- s 154(1)(a)(i): offence involving fraud/dishonesty punishable >= 3 months
-- s 154(3): automatic 5-year disqualification
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 154(1),(3)"
GIVEN `convicted of fraud or dishonesty offence`  IS A BOOLEAN
    , `offence punishable with imprisonment months` IS A NUMBER
    , `subject to SFA civil penalty`               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `automatically disqualified as director` IF
        (`convicted of fraud or dishonesty offence`
            AND `offence punishable with imprisonment months` AT LEAST 3)
    OR  `subject to SFA civil penalty`

-- s 154(3): disqualification period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 154(3)"
`automatic disqualification period years` MEANS 5


§§§ `s 155 — Disqualification for persistent default`

-- s 155(1),(3): disqualification if 3+ offences/orders within 5 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155(1),(3)"
GIVEN `relevant offences or orders` IS A NUMBER
    , `within 5 year window`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `persistently in default` IF
    `relevant offences or orders` AT LEAST 3
    AND `within 5 year window`

-- s 155(1): disqualification period after last offence/order
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155(1)"
`persistent default disqualification years` MEANS 5

-- s 155(1): penalty
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155(1)"
`penalty for persistent default` MEANS 10000
`imprisonment for persistent default years` MEANS 2


§§§ `s 155A — Disqualification for struck-off companies`

-- s 155A(1): director of 3+ companies struck off within 5 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155A(1)"
GIVEN `companies struck off` IS A NUMBER
    , `within 5 year period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disqualified for struck off companies` IF
    `companies struck off` AT LEAST 3
    AND `within 5 year period`

-- s 155A(1A): disqualification period
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155A(1A)"
GIVEN `previously disqualified under s155A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `struck off disqualification period years` IS
    IF `previously disqualified under s155A`
    THEN 5
    ELSE 3


§§§ `s 155B — Debarment order conditions`

-- s 155B(4): conditions for making debarment order
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 155B(4)"
GIVEN `default persisted months`   IS A NUMBER
    , `was director or secretary`  IS A BOOLEAN
    , `notice given days`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `debarment order conditions met` IF
        `default persisted months` AT LEAST 3
    AND `was director or secretary`
    AND `notice given days` AT LEAST 14


§§§ `s 163 — Connected-company loan threshold`

-- s 163(1): director(s) interested in >= 20% of voting power
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 163(1)"
GIVEN `director voting power pct in entity` IS A NUMBER
    , `is exempt private company`           IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `connected company loan requires approval` IF
    `director voting power pct in entity` AT LEAST 20
    AND NOT `is exempt private company`


§§§ `s 164A — Director emolument disclosure`

-- s 164A(1): threshold for member demand
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 164A(1)"
GIVEN `percentage of total members`    IS A NUMBER
    , `percentage of issued shares`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may demand director emolument disclosure` IF
    `percentage of total members` AT LEAST 10
    OR `percentage of issued shares` AT LEAST 5

-- s 164A(2),(3): preparation and circulation deadlines
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 164A(2)–(3)"
`emolument statement preparation days` MEANS 14
`emolument statement circulation days` MEANS 14


§§ `Division 3 — Meetings and proceedings`


§§§ `s 175 — Annual general meeting`

-- s 175(1): AGM deadline after end of financial year
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 175(1)"
GIVEN `is listed public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `AGM deadline months after financial year end` IS
    IF `is listed public company`
    THEN 4
    ELSE 6

-- s 175(4): penalty for non-compliance
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 175(4)"
`penalty for AGM non compliance` MEANS 5000


§§§ `s 176 — EGM on member requisition`

-- s 176(1): requisition threshold — 10% of paid-up voting shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 176(1)"
GIVEN `percentage of paid up voting shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may requisition EGM` IF
    `percentage of paid up voting shares` AT LEAST 10

-- s 176(1): directors must convene within 2 months
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 176(1)"
`EGM convening deadline months` MEANS 2

-- s 176(3): directors' failure window — 21 days
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 176(3)"
`EGM director failure window days` MEANS 21

-- s 176(3): requisitionists holding > 50% of total requisitionist votes may convene
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 176(3)"
GIVEN `requisitionist voting pct of total requisitionists` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `requisitionists may convene EGM` IF
    `requisitionist voting pct of total requisitionists` GREATER THAN 50

-- s 176(3): meeting must not be held after 3 months from requisition
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 176(3)"
`EGM maximum months from requisition` MEANS 3


§§§ `s 183 — Member requisition to circulate resolutions`

-- s 183(2): threshold for requisition
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 183(2)"
GIVEN `percentage of total voting rights` IS A NUMBER
    , `number of members`                 IS A NUMBER
    , `average paid up per member`        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may requisition resolution circulation` IF
    `percentage of total voting rights` AT LEAST 5
    OR (`number of members` AT LEAST 100
        AND `average paid up per member` AT LEAST 500)

-- s 183(3): timing requirements
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 183(3)"
`resolution notice lead time weeks` MEANS 6
`statement circulation lead time weeks` MEANS 1


§§§ `s 184 — Special resolution requirements`

-- s 184(1): notice period depends on company type
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 184(1)"
GIVEN c IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `special resolution notice days` c IS
    IF c's `classification` EQUALS `private company`
    THEN 14
    ELSE 21

-- s 184(1): majority threshold — 75%
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 184(1)"
`special resolution majority pct` MEANS 75

-- s 184(2): short-notice waiver — 95% of total voting rights must agree
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 184(2)"
`short notice waiver threshold pct` MEANS 95


§§§ `s 184DA — Written resolution lapse`

-- s 184DA(1): lapses after 28 days from circulation
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 184DA(1)"
`written resolution lapse days` MEANS 28


§§ `Division 5 — Annual return`


§§§ `s 197 — Annual return deadline`

-- s 197(1),(2): lodge annual return within 30 days of AGM
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 197(1)"
`annual return lodgement days after AGM` MEANS 30


§§§ `s 199 — Accounting records retention`

-- s 199(1): records kept for >= 5 years
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 199(1)"
`accounting records retention years` MEANS 5


